# TODO

## 1. Gripper reach
- [x] Shrink the suction reach: the distance from the cup tips (gripper_tcp)
      to the object surface at which suction grabs - gripper_manager's
      suction_reach (group_a_bringup/launch/bringup.launch.py arg): 0.06 -> 0.01 m

## 2. workcell_demo package
- [x] New package src/workcell/workcell_demo: the main orchestrator for the
      system's later high-level functionality (state machine node + launch)

## 3. Navigator action servers
- [x] Action interfaces in custom_msgs: NavigateToNode (graph path to a node
      id/label), CartesianMove (straight-line tool offset); gripper: existing
      gripper/set_suction + new latched gripper/state (GripperState)
- [x] navigator_cli: ROS 2 node serving them (same graph / robot manager as the
      CLI), so the demo and other scripts can call navigation over messages
- [x] shared_utils: NavigatorClient wrapping those interfaces for easy access
      from any script

## 4. Navigator CLI gripper command
- [x] `g on|off` / `gripper on|off` command in navigator_cli

## 5. Demo pick & place cycle (workcell_demo)
When a box is at the beam, the robot is idle and holding nothing:
- [x] navigate to node 6
- [x] cartesian move 10 cm down
- [x] gripper on
- [x] cartesian move 10 cm up
- [x] navigate to one of the place nodes 2 / 3 / 4
- [x] gripper off
- [x] navigate back to node 5 (idle), wait for the next box

## Follow-ups
- [ ] Pick height: with a 1 cm suction reach, a fixed 10 cm descent from node 6
      (tool at z=0.66, belt top 0.40) only reaches boxes ~0.15-0.17 m tall -
      boxes are 0.08-0.25 m. Descend by the waiting box's height instead
      (factory publishes sizes on /box_factory/spawned), or a guarded
      move-until-contact.
- [ ] Try the full cycle live in Gazebo (only tested against fakes so far).
